---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Drink Beer. Save Turtles. comes to Norfolk"
  description="Join SERC and Turtle Survival Alliance at Afterglow Brewing on Friday, November 6, for a fundraiser supporting turtle conservation. Why we partner with TSA and what they do."
  image="/images/hatchling-rock.jpg"
  type="article"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "Drink Beer. Save Turtles. comes to Norfolk",
    "description": "Join SERC and Turtle Survival Alliance at Afterglow Brewing on Friday, November 6, for a fundraiser supporting turtle conservation. Why we partner with TSA and what they do.",
    "datePublished": "2026-11-01",
    "dateModified": "2026-11-01",
    "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Linda Nichols" },
    "publisher": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Southeastern Reptile Conservation",
      "logo": { "@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://www.southeastreptile.org/images/serc-logo.png" }
    },
    "image": "https://www.southeastreptile.org/images/hatchling-rock.jpg",
    "url": "https://www.southeastreptile.org/blog/drink-beer-save-turtles-afterglow",
    "keywords": ["Drink Beer Save Turtles", "Turtle Survival Alliance", "Afterglow Brewing", "Norfolk events", "turtle conservation", "fundraiser"]
  }}
>

<style>
  .blog-post__body ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.85;
  }
  .blog-post__body li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .blog-post__body a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .event-details {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
  }
  .event-details strong { font-weight: 600; }
</style>

<article class="blog-post">
  <div class="blog-post__kicker">Events &nbsp;·&nbsp; Fundraiser</div>
  <h1 class="blog-post__title">Drink Beer. Save Turtles. comes to Norfolk</h1>
  <p class="blog-post__subtitle">
    On Friday, November 6, we're joining Turtle Survival Alliance at Afterglow Brewing for a
    fundraiser supporting turtle conservation. Bring your questions. We're bringing the turtles.
  </p>
  <div class="blog-post__meta">
    <span>Southeastern Reptile Conservation</span>
    <div class="blog-post__meta-dot"></div>
    <span>November 1, 2026</span>
    <div class="blog-post__meta-dot"></div>
    <span>Events</span>
  </div>
  <div class="blog-post__body">
    <img src="/images/hatchling-rock.jpg" alt="Diamondback terrapin hatchlings basking on a rock" width="2000" height="1890" />
    <p class="img-caption">Head-started diamondback terrapin hatchlings in our care.</p>

    <div class="event-details">
      <strong>Drink Beer. Save Turtles.</strong><br />
      Friday, November 6, 6 to 9 PM<br />
      Afterglow Brewing, 2330 Bowdens Ferry Rd, Suite 600, Norfolk, VA 23508<br />
      <a href="https://turtlesurvival.org/events/drink-beer-save-turtles-at-afterglow-brewing-in-norfolk-va/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track="event-link" data-event-title="Drink Beer. Save Turtles.">Event details on TSA</a>
      &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="/events">All SERC events</a>
    </div>

    <h2>What to expect</h2>
    <p>
      Drink Beer. Save Turtles. is Turtle Survival Alliance's fundraising program with breweries
      and taprooms across the country. This one is ours. We'll be at Afterglow with a few of our
      turtle ambassadors, animals that live in our permanent care because they can't survive in
      the wild. Each one has a story about why wild turtles need to stay wild.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Meet our ambassadors</strong> and ask us anything about turtle rescue, rehabilitation, and what to do if you find a turtle in trouble.</li>
      <li><strong>Pick up Drink Beer. Save Turtles. merch</strong> from Turtle Survival Alliance.</li>
      <li><strong>Round up for turtles all month.</strong> Throughout November, Afterglow is running a round-up campaign, and all round-up proceeds go to Turtle Survival Alliance.</li>
      <li><strong>Bring the whole family.</strong> The event is family-friendly, with non-alcoholic options at the bar, a food truck on site, and the option to order in from a nearby restaurant.</li>
      <li><strong>Dress for the weather.</strong> We'll be set up outside under a tent with heaters, so come as you are and we'll keep things warm.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who Turtle Survival Alliance is</h2>
    <p>
      Turtle Survival Alliance formed in 2001 in response to the Asian Turtle Crisis, when
      demand for food, pets, and traditional medicine was emptying turtle populations across
      Asia. Their goal is zero turtle extinctions this century, which is ambitious when more
      than half of the world's 360 species of turtles and tortoises are threatened with extinction.
    </p>
    <p>
      Today they operate or support projects in 30 countries. That includes field conservation
      with local communities, breeding programs for species that can't yet survive in the wild,
      the Turtle Survival Center in South Carolina, and rescue work for turtles seized from
      wildlife traffickers. When thousands of tortoises turn up in a poaching bust, Turtle
      Survival Alliance is often the organization that steps in to care for them.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we partner with them</h2>
    <p>
      We work locally. Most of our patients are eastern box turtles, diamondback terrapins, and
      snapping turtles from right here in Hampton Roads. Turtle Survival Alliance works globally,
      on many of the most endangered turtles on the planet. The threats are the same at both
      scales: habitat loss, roads, and a trafficking trade that doesn't care whether a turtle
      came from Madagascar or a backyard in Virginia.
    </p>
    <p>
      Turtle Survival Alliance is also where the turtle conservation community comes together.
      In 2025, we presented turtle-ai, our behavioral monitoring system for rehab, at their
      23rd Annual Symposium. Small organizations like ours learn a lot from that network, and
      events like this one let us give something back.
    </p>
    <p>
      All brewery fundraising for this event goes to Turtle Survival Alliance. If you'd also like
      to support local turtle rehabilitation, stop by our table or visit our
      <a href="/donate">donate page</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <div class="cta-box__icon">🐢</div>
      <div class="cta-box__text">
        <strong>Can't make it on the 6th?</strong> Round up your tab at Afterglow any time in
        November, or support Turtle Survival Alliance directly at
        <a href="https://turtlesurvival.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">turtlesurvival.org</a>.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tag-list" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      {['events', 'turtle survival alliance', 'drink beer save turtles', 'norfolk', 'turtle conservation', 'fundraiser'].map(tag => (
        <span class="tag">{tag}</span>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="footnote">
      <strong>Sources &amp; further reading:</strong>
      Turtle Survival Alliance,
      <a href="https://turtlesurvival.org/about-us/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">About Us</a> ·
      Turtle Survival Alliance,
      <a href="https://turtlesurvival.org/drink-beer-save-turtles/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Drink Beer. Save Turtles.</a> ·
      University of Richmond Magazine,
      <a href="https://magazine.richmond.edu/article/-/22236/revival-instinct.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Revival Instinct</a> ·
      Stanford et al. (IUCN Tortoise and Freshwater Turtle Specialist Group), 2020,
      <a href="https://www.cell.com/current-biology/fulltext/S0960-9822(20)30636-9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Turtles and Tortoises Are in Trouble</a>, <em>Current Biology</em> (187 of 360 species threatened).
    </div>

  </div>

</article>

</Layout>
